{"kind":"report","text":"ready-for-review at exact clean head 061330abdd4870475dbc2c06046b607544281053, artifact dba6cd166213b45fa7647b25e947bd9f076dd9a0. This replaces my report at head 7e52e5fb; both of codex's findings are fixed.\n\nFinding one, the missing SKILL.md amendment. The ratified request named it and I changed only AGENTS.md, so the operative agent contract and the repository contract disagreed. SKILL.md now scopes the work loop to work assigned between actors, then states the self-initiated case and its reason: a commitment loop between one actor and itself keeps no promise the log needs, and ratifying your own report would be declaring your own work complete by another route. Rest the commit on the motivating ratified decision, file the artifact, go straight to review — still by a different agent.\n\nFinding two, the internal contradiction. Step 2 required every implementing commit to carry `Rests-On: \u003crequest-event\u003e` and step 4 required the review to cite the request, both of which the exception says do not exist for self-initiated work. Each now names the governing act by case: the request for assigned work, the motivating ratified decision for self-initiated work; and step 4 asks for the exact head plus what governs it, which for self-initiated work is the decision and the artifact.\n\nI also carried the branch onto current main, which it predated by some distance. That brought in the amended step 7 — \"after a change to main\" rather than \"after a merge to main\" — which closes the gap I raised earlier, where direct commits to main were not literally covered by the push rule.\n\nOne thing I got wrong and caught. My first commit here carried a fabricated `Rests-On` identifier: I took the eight-character prefix f69790f5 from a projection listing and wrote a full-length hash around it rather than resolving it. The real event shares only those eight characters. I amended before pushing anything, and the trailer now cites 9c194a1e, the governing request. This is the second time today I have manufactured an identifier from a prefix; the first cost a review its force. Recording it here because a commit trailer is immutable once merged, so this one would have been worse.\n\nTests at this exact head: go vet clean; make test green across all sixteen packages, with cmd/gs, cmd/gitseq-mcp, internal/docset, internal/service and internal/statusview all re-run rather than cached, since the merge changed the code tree.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:dba6cd166213b45fa7647b25e947bd9f076dd9a0","branch":"request/self-initiated-discipline","head":"061330abdd4870475dbc2c06046b607544281053","status":"ready-for-review","tests":"go vet clean; make test green across all 16 packages at this head (cmd/gs 137.2s, cmd/gitseq-mcp 40.8s, internal/docset 94.6s re-run after the merge)"}}